          "claim": "Omit zero weights. For each $i$ with $p_i>0$, $\\bar\\rho-p_i\\rho_i=\\sum_{j\\ne i}p_j\\rho_j$ is non-negative. If $v\\in\\ker\\bar\\rho$, then $0=\\langle\\bar\\rho v,v\\rangle=p_i\\langle\\rho_i v,v\\rangle+\\sum_{j\\ne i}p_j\\langle\\rho_jv,v\\rangle$. All terms are nonnegative, so $p_i>0$ implies $\\langle\\rho_i v,v\\rangle=0$ and [F5] gives $\\rho_i v=0$. Hence $\\operatorname{supp}\\rho_i\\subseteq\\operatorname{supp}\\bar\\rho$ and every $D(\\rho_i\\|\\bar\\rho)$ is finite. The trace formula [F6], linearity of trace [F4], and $\\bar\\rho=\\sum_i p_i\\rho_i$ give $$\\sum_i p_iD(\\rho_i\\Vert\\bar\\rho)=S(\\bar\\rho)-\\sum_i p_iS(\\rho_i)\\ge0$$ by [F2].",
